{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials","id":629063,"title":"What if The Solars never killed any of the Primordials?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-16T14:33:16-07:00","id":629063,"title":"What if The Solars never killed any of the Primordials?","content":"With the upcoming release of 3E I've been rereading 2E material after taking a long hiatus from the game. I was thinking of Alternate Exalted Universes and wondered as the question says - what if in the Primordial War the solars never killed any of the Primordials - thereby never created any Neverborn?<br /> <br /> This to me requires some kind of deliberate or intentional strategy on the part of the Gods and Solars, as I understand it, canon points out that the concept of the consequences of killing them wasn't even conceived of until they killed the first few.<br /> <br /> For Prehistory, this implies a few other changes:<br /> <br /> 1.) The Primordial War may have lasted longer as it removed one of the points of leverage to force a surrender<br /> <br /> 2.) The Exalted host may have had to wait longer and grow larger - possibly tipping off the Primordials that something was going to happen.<br /> <br /> 3.) They may have deployed some other kind of weapon or artifact to control a primordial by controlling it's 2nd and 3rd Circle Souls. (not sure if possible, mind you.)<br /> <br /> In the First Age:<br /> <br /> 1.) With no Neverborn, there would be no Necromancy, nor would it be possible to create shadowlands. <br /> <br /> 2.) The Great Curse could be worse if more Primordials were alive to Curse the Exalted Host<br /> <br /> 3.) Related to #1, there may have been more escaped Primordials who attacked Creation. The premise implies that these Primordials are also not killed, perhaps forced somehow into Malfeas.<br /> <br /> 4.) When/if the Sidereals killed all the Solars and some of the Lunars, there would be no DeathLords created.<br /> <br /> 5.) No Great Contagion (since no Underworld and Deathlords) means that the Shogunate endures much longer - perhaps it collapses from repeated FairFolk incursions. <br /> <br /> <br /> What other thoughts do people have here on this idea? I'm curious to see where it go to create alternate settings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T14:38:54-07:00","id":629105,"title":"","content":"It would have been hard, I think, to defeat the Primordials. You could fetich death them, but they'd just keep coming back over and over. Off hand, I imagine that the Primordial War never would have finished, and the Exalted hosts would be defending themselves against Primordial aggression to this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T14:54:45-07:00","id":629110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials#post629063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) The Great Curse could be worse if more Primordials were alive to Curse the Exalted Host</div> </div> </div> </div>The Great Curse was actually made by the dying primordials, not the living. So no Neverborn means no great curse - at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","name":"Owill0w","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T16:18:41-07:00","id":629160,"title":"","content":"Things probably wouldn't have gotten as bad at least no where near as quickly as it did. I mean the Usurpation happened because the Sids started to notice that the Solars were going utterly insane and possibly becoming a threat to the world. No dead Primordials means no Great Curse means fewer Solars go insane and even then they might not reach the same heights of utter crazy that forced the Sids hands.<br /> <br /> You'd have a lot more demons though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T17:28:54-07:00","id":629266,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure this was ever possible. The alpha strike of the Titanomachy was on the fetich of the Lidless Eye that Sees, with the explicit goal of knocking out the Primordials' premier ability to gather intelligence and to cause a ton of confusing by imploding it. Take that away and it becomes less likely for the rebels to succeed at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T17:45:56-07:00","id":629293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629266#post629266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure this was ever possible. The alpha strike of the Titanomachy was on the fetich of the Lidless Eye that Sees, with the explicit goal of knocking out the Primordials' premier ability to gather intelligence and to cause a ton of confusing by imploding it. Take that away and it becomes less likely for the rebels to succeed at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OP isn't that the Exalted couldn't Fetch kill the Primordials, but that they didn't double kill them into Neverborn.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I see there being two possibilities.<br /> <br /> 1) Exalted Host wins, Malfeas happens, etc. Things would probably be better all around for Creation. No Noberborn, no Great Curse. No Great Curse means that the insanity of the Exalted becomes the minority rather than the majority, thus no need for a Great Prophecy or Usurpation. First Age is probably still kicking and while things aren't perfect, they aren't the Second Age.<br /> <br /> 2) Both sides fight each other to a draw. The conflict could still be going &quot;Hot&quot; with open warfare happening, aka the Primordial War itself being the setting. Or it could have gone &quot;cold&quot;, both sides agreeing to a cease fire(possibly involving the Exalted gaining a section of undiminished Creation for themselves, possibly making their own damn Creation with blackjack and hookers), meanwhile all matters of skullduggery going on as the Primordials and Exalts jockey for position without breaking the rules of their treaties. Basically, the Cold War, only with more magical demigods and god-monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T18:35:20-07:00","id":629366,"title":"","content":"Fetich killing the Lidless Eye may not have been enough. Themes don't change THAT much from what we've seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T19:19:58-07:00","id":629407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629366#post629366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetich killing the Lidless Eye may not have been enough. Themes don't change THAT much from what we've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> The OP question is &quot;What if the Exalted didn't kill any Primordials?&quot; Not &quot;What if the Exalted couldn't kill any Primordials?&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus, it's not like they Neverborned him in canon. They killed his Fetich, and the Lidless Eye turned into Sach, who's themes haven't really changed much.<br /> <br /> The Lidless Eye saw almost everything(aside from the Exalts coming to gank his Fetich), Sach does see everything, but what he sees depends on whether he's awake or asleep. Asleep, he sees the present, awake the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T20:09:03-07:00","id":629451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629407#post629407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?<br /> <br /> The OP question is &quot;What if the Exalted didn't kill any Primordials?&quot; Not &quot;What if the Exalted couldn't kill any Primordials?&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus, it's not like they Neverborned him in canon. They killed his Fetich, and the Lidless Eye turned into Sach, who's themes haven't really changed much.<br /> <br /> The Lidless Eye saw almost everything(aside from the Exalts coming to gank his Fetich), Sach does see everything, but what he sees depends on whether he's awake or asleep. Asleep, he sees the present, awake the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Sach went to sleep the same instant he became Sach,so that part of the equation plays out basically the same.<br /> <br /> A point I'd like to know. The Neverborn weren't specifically targeted to be destroyed correct? I mean I know the premise here is what if they didn't Neverborn any of them and in canon it wasn't a fully known detail that a Primordial could die before it happened. But I mean the ones who did die weren't targeted more than most of the others correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T20:44:12-07:00","id":629476,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem you run into with this thought exercise is that one of the major movers and shakers of the Exalted Antagonist Team is removed with nothing to take its place. <br /> <br /> Without the Neverborn, no Great Curse emerges, so it's theoretically possible that Solar excesses never grow as grand or terrible. And it's possible that the Great Prophecy, if it happens, plays out differently.<br /> <br /> If the Usurpation happens, it ends on a different note, perhaps less desparately.<br /> <br /> Also, the Yozis have little power to touch the world, and it was only through dealings with the Deathlords that the Jade Prison was broken.<br /> <br /> But let's toy with things, a bit:<br /> <br /> The Primordials never died, so as a result, the cycle of reincarnation remains perfect. Or, as some Lawgivers would say, &quot;perfect.&quot; With the quotes. After all, perfect reincarnation means that their death is the end of them, entirely, everything that they were wiped away and clean, burning away in Lethe like an elaborate tapestry cast into a forge.<br /> <br /> This is unacceptable. But, they must admit, there is no soul powerful enough to cling to existence on its own.<br /> <br /> So one must be made. Through sorcery, patience, and the dreams of thousands, something resembling a consciousness takes form, and is cast metaphysically into the burning river of dead souls. It cannot be burned away by the reincarnation of souls, for it was never born. And it never will be. Such an anomaly might still just be pulled away from any real contact with Creation, but it clings to the place of its making. It hurts badly--alas, in Lethe it is easier to hold onto darker passions than lighter ones--but cannot bring itself to let go. The Solars who made it have seen to that. The Lawgivers have also seen to the special rites before and after their own last breaths, and when they die their souls do not burn clean, but travel along the black cord tethering the suffering seed of their posthumous paradise to this world. Each of the Chosen gets their own seed, their own personal kingdom to sculpt in their image after death.<br /> <br /> Some few are powerful enough to gaze into these foreign worlds, though none have yet discerned a way in, and while the temptation to ensure an immortality existing beyond the mere records of history is tempting, the most sagacious among them are cautious. Setting aside the practical difficulties and ethics both in the concept of forgoing the natural order, as well as forging these ersatz world-entities with real suffering, there are questions as to whether this poses some potential harm to the flow of reincarnation, or--posit the most conservative voices--to Creation itself. There are rumors that some of the lands of these self-styled Lords of the Dead have accrued souls there by accident rather than design, and while the shapeless things at the heart of these worlds may not enter Creation, they would certainly try had they the strength. There may be a critical mass, some theorize, beyond which there may be no turning back.<br /> <br /> And yet, say too many of those gray-headed oldest among the Chosen, feeling their mortality about them, one more couldn't possibly hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T22:12:38-07:00","id":629557,"title":"","content":"Oh interesting point. The only soulsteel that would exist would be those things that cheesed Auto off badly enough that he forged them into it. I mean the soulsteel forged by Exalts and all requires rock from the Underworld and ghosts. Both of which become a might trickier to acquire in a world that never had the Underworld invented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T01:05:44-07:00","id":629686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629293#post629293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Both sides fight each other to a draw. The conflict could still be going &quot;Hot&quot; with open warfare happening, aka the Primordial War itself being the setting. Or it could have gone &quot;cold&quot;, both sides agreeing to a cease fire(possibly involving the Exalted gaining a section of undiminished Creation for themselves, possibly making their own damn Creation with blackjack and hookers), meanwhile all matters of skullduggery going on as the Primordials and Exalts jockey for position without breaking the rules of their treaties. Basically, the Cold War, only with more magical demigods and god-monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that could make a great Shard. Cold-war style shenanigans between the Exalted Host and the Demon Hordes, gods shifting alliances between the two... Spycraft and proxy wars and space-race-like intimidation (Ligier and his servants on one side, the Twilights on the other, building montruous weapons and wyld-breaching ships to deliver them... sorry, &quot;explore the unending possibilities of Chaos.&quot;, stealing blueprints from one-another...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:26:41-07:00","id":629844,"title":"","content":"Obvious-ish but not yet mentioned - Autocthon has probably stuck around in Creation, since it was the combination of the shock of his siblings deaths and his awareness of the Curse that drove him to flee in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:41:02-07:00","id":629853,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a great Shard for more natural and constant contact with Demons and Alchemicals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T07:12:11-07:00","id":629885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629853#post629853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a great Shard for more natural and constant contact with Demons and Alchemicals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, demon-summoning probably wouldn't be a thing, because there wouldn't be surrender oaths, and peaceful colaboration would probably draw heavy suspicion, because, y'know, they're the enemy in that cold war you're not-fighting. During the cold war, &quot;the communists&quot; were what terrorists are today.<br /> <br /> But Alchemicals might be casual encounters, yah.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T07:31:42-07:00","id":629901,"title":"","content":"I like both major possibilities raised in the thread; that is,<br /> <br /> A) All Primordials bound as Yozi other than Gaia and Autochthon, with the nascent Underworld (and maybe Deathlords) the result of Exalted hubris sans Great Curse,<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> B) Primordial War several centuries or millennia in the making, with hot and cold phases.<br /> <br /> Both are very fertile ground for Shards, to second what others have said. Both also allow for Alchemicals in Creation in ways that don't require shoehorning the Locust Crusade out of the way (assuming that shows back up in however many years, anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T16:13:40-07:00","id":630376,"title":"","content":"Wow - great discussion guys!<br /> <br /> I like the idea of &quot;the long war&quot; a war of attrition of some kind between Creation &amp; the Primordials. Perhaps they've even forced a few Primordials to surrender, but the majority are still free. It would make for a bit of a paranoid Creation, where everyone knows that at any given time, the Primordials could attack again, but just don't know when it will be. Infiltration of the other side would be definitely be a thing. <br /> <br /> Another problem may exist - since Exalts would be dying much, much more frequently Solars would not be attaining the level of power seen in the Canon Fight Age and would likely have less powerful artifacts and advances in their civilization.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T07:42:10-07:00","id":632269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629160#post629160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things probably wouldn't have gotten as bad at least no where near as quickly as it did. I mean the Usurpation happened because the Sids started to notice that the Solars were going utterly insane and possibly becoming a threat to the world. No dead Primordials means no Great Curse means fewer Solars go insane and even then they might not reach the same heights of utter crazy that forced the Sids hands.<br /> <br /> You'd have a lot more demons though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have always wondered how much the setting wants to make me think that it is the great curse that made Solars power mad, paranoid, crazy despotic rulers.<br /> <br /> To me it has always been rather minor and the actual commentary has been on absolute power corrupts absolutely rather than the curse making it happen. This fit better with the theme of exalted for me where the big meat of the game coneptually is how you will deal with that power this time round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T15:46:17-07:00","id":632791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=632269#post632269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always wondered how much the setting wants to make me think that it is the great curse that made Solars power mad, paranoid, crazy despotic rulers.<br /> <br /> To me it has always been rather minor and the actual commentary has been on absolute power corrupts absolutely rather than the curse making it happen. This fit better with the theme of exalted for me where the big meat of the game coneptually is how you will deal with that power this time round.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting can absolutely not answer this question one way or another - &quot;the great curse made em do it&quot; leads to the conclusion &quot;oh, so if we purify exaltation somehow, then there will be no problem at all by being ruled by nigh-immortal godkings,&quot; and &quot;no, it was just human nature&quot; is a <i>deeply</i> pessimistic statement that turns the setting shitdark.<br /> <br /> It's in the between-spaces where the life of the game can happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:05:36-07:00","id":632834,"title":"","content":"What if they only ever killed 1 Primordial, and it was The Dragon's Shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/818-stephan1864","name":"Stephan1864","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:22:12-07:00","id":632844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always wondered how much the setting wants to make me think that it is the great curse</div> </div> </div> </div> Grabowski put statements of attributing the fall of the First Age to the Great Curse in the outlines. This was in no way a commentary on what a setting without the Great Curse would be like, except in so far as to make options feel available. (That is an objective fact, and so the extent of what I'll say. This topic makes me sleepy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:25:31-07:00","id":632846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=632791#post632791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The setting can absolutely not answer this question one way or another - &amp;quot;the great curse made em do it&amp;quot; leads to the conclusion &amp;quot;oh, so if we purify exaltation somehow, then there will be no problem at all by being ruled by nigh-immortal godkings,&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;no, it was just human nature&amp;quot; is a <i>deeply</i> pessimistic statement that turns the setting shitdark.<br /> <br /> It's in the between-spaces where the life of the game can happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it gets to shitdark, but it certainly is a pessimistic take on human nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:30:33-07:00","id":632850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629293#post629293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP isn't that the Exalted couldn't Fetch kill the Primordials, but that they didn't double kill them into Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=629407#post629407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP question is &amp;quot;What if the Exalted didn't kill any Primordials?&amp;quot; Not &amp;quot;What if the Exalted couldn't kill any Primordials?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I posit that if there had been no permakilling there would be no threat to force the Primordials to surrender. The Exalted likely wouldn't know that they could even do so, having no experience to show otherwise, or at the very least wouldn't know the result. If they hadn't implemented permakilling it implies they were not willing to deal with whatever hypothetical consequences it could cause and were unwilling to roll the dice and see. <br /> <br /> I don't think the war would be winnable in that situation because the Exalted would lack leverage beyond &quot;we will change your forms and annoy you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:38:49-07:00","id":632854,"title":"","content":"I'd say it depends on exactly what one means by &quot;corrupts&quot;; behavioral and neurological science has accumulated a lot of evidence that authority and responsibilities tend to have certain &quot;negative&quot; effects on personalities, but I feel as though historical and contemporary example might suggest that this is not necessarily something to cause despair. Not as a &quot;you need hard people to make the difficult decisions&quot; and more of a... becoming a bit of a jerk doesn't necessarily mean you're bad at your job, or that you'll actually do it to any worse ends. It's like... if you were rescued by a firefighter who turned out to be quite a jerk as a person, would it make you any less saved by a fire? Would you demand to be put into the fire until a nice firefighter saved you? It doesn't necessarily intersect, does it. I'd say that all Exalted wind up becoming some degree of corrupt, and it's not often the problem of anybody but themselves and those closest to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T20:37:26-07:00","id":633006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=632850#post632850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then I posit that if there had been no permakilling there would be no threat to force the Primordials to surrender. The Exalted likely wouldn't know that they could even do so, having no experience to show otherwise, or at the very least wouldn't know the result. If they hadn't implemented permakilling it implies they were not willing to deal with whatever hypothetical consequences it could cause and were unwilling to roll the dice and see.<br /> <br /> I don't think the war would be winnable in that situation because the Exalted would lack leverage beyond &quot;we will change your forms and annoy you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't fetich death always lead to diminishment? Change their forms and annoy them could eventually push all the titans down to sickly Autochthon's level, while maintaining their own power and potential. Based on the Aftershock Primordial and possibly gunstar the Exalted might be able to convert Titans into allies, weaklings, or slaves given enough time and violent soul surgery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:14:14-07:00","id":633082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=633006#post633006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't fetich death always lead to diminishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetich death always leads to <i>change</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:16:41-07:00","id":633086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=633082#post633082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetich death always leads to <i>change</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it just the Demon Emperor who the progression was explicit fore? The Empyreal Chaos -&gt; the Demon City -&gt; The dim red star? (I forget where that last one comes from but have seen it more than once.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:32:58-07:00","id":633115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=632850#post632850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I posit that if there had been no permakilling there would be no threat to force the Primordials to surrender. The Exalted likely wouldn't know that they could even do so, having no experience to show otherwise, or at the very least wouldn't know the result. If they hadn't implemented permakilling it implies they were not willing to deal with whatever hypothetical consequences it could cause and were unwilling to roll the dice and see.<br /> <br /> I don't think the war would be winnable in that situation because the Exalted would lack leverage beyond &quot;we will change your forms and annoy you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I haven't read the material in ages, but I don't recall the Primordials regarding fetich death as no big deal. It would just be hard for me to swallow if they did. Looking at Adorjan next to Adrian and Sacheverell next to Lidless Eye That Sees... I have trouble conceiving of the Primordials interpreting that in any way other than, &quot;Holy shit!&quot; It is a cessation of self in just about every way that's likely to matter to them. They cease to be, and some other jerk walks off with their Essence, having reshuffled their themes and motifs around. If they have for comparison the complete existential agony that is becoming a Neverborn on the table, sure, I could maybe see it coming off as favorable, but, well... It's not, for the purposes of this thread.<br /> <br /> Hell, do we even have any reason to think <i>fetich death</i> ever even happened before the Primordial War? There's no mention. And the Primordials aren't merely presented as unkillable but as more-or-less <i>unassailable</i> before the Exalted came along. I could imagine that fetich death alone would be a pretty sobering discovery. The Exalted could inflict it on them and in a rather distressing quantity. Fighting a foe that just keeps coming, and proves very capable of bringing on an awful degeneration in more and more of your siblings, and it becomes increasingly clear that it could be just a matter of chance and time until that could happen to you...<br /> <br /> I expect the Primordial War would have dragged on longer, some more Primordials would have become other than we know them before it ended, and the terms might have been less unpleasant for them. But I don't have difficulty believing the Primordials might have ultimately surrendered. It's not necessarily what would have happened, but I find it very conceivable based on what we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:34:07-07:00","id":633118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=633006#post633006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't fetich death always lead to diminishment? Change their forms and annoy them could eventually push all the titans down to sickly Autochthon's level, while maintaining their own power and potential. Based on the Aftershock Primordial and possibly gunstar the Exalted might be able to convert Titans into allies, weaklings, or slaves given enough time and violent soul surgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the alteration is rather unpredictable and the amount of power they have gets kind of crazy. I mean Satch is considered and existence level threat by the other Yozi just because he might wake up and no one wants to know what happens if they force him to change again in case it gets worse. I mean god help you if the all devouring gorge became She Who Live's new fetich after her old one's death and the Pyre in which thoughts are burned becomes the All Consuming Pyre or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:51:38-07:00","id":633132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=633118#post633118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that the alteration is rather unpredictable and the amount of power they have gets kind of crazy. I mean Satch is considered and existence level threat by the other Yozi just because he might wake up and no one wants to know what happens if they force him to change again in case it gets worse. I mean god help you if the all devouring gorge became She Who Live's new fetich after her old one's death and the Pyre in which thoughts are burned becomes the All Consuming Pyre or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can apparently be guided to some extent, but Remantheus and the Gunstar indicate that exerting any sort of control takes a long time and a lot of care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:15:46-07:00","id":633175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=633132#post633132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can apparently be guided to some extent, but Remantheus and the Gunstar indicate that exerting any sort of control takes a long time and a lot of care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall who Remantheus was, so I could be wrong on that point. However Gunstar was not a case of fetich death. They killed one of Auto's 3rd circles but the others were modified not slain and the one they killed wasn't Auto's fetich, so it just led to alterations in Auto's mindset not a restructuring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:20:44-07:00","id":633180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/629063-what-if-the-solars-never-killed-any-of-the-primordials?p=633175#post633175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't recall who Remantheus was, so I could be wrong on that point. However Gunstar was not a case of fetich death. They killed one of Auto's 3rd circles but the others were modified not slain and the one they killed wasn't Auto's fetich, so it just led to alterations in Auto's mindset not a restructuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ramethus is the real spelling, my memory failed me. He/it was the Aftershock Primordial, who ran away after the war and transformed himself into the ultimate war Titan.<br /> <br /> In Gunstar, it was the bigger plan to eventually kill the Core and transform Autochthon into the Gunstar, a war machine primordial rather than the great maker. All the other stuff was build up so that the reforming primordial would be what they wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}